Third-party components
----------------------

None. Hearth has no third-party dependency and no CDN.

Vendored from this project's own kits (same licence, same author), copied verbatim on 26/11/2026:

- web-kit 0.1.0 — docs/play/web-kit.js — the offline shell, storage helpers and PWA registration
- export-kit 1.0.0 — docs/play/export-kit.js — Blob download, used for the home export

Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

What is not built
-----------------

mDNS discovery and real device control. A LAN transport does exist in this estate (lan-kit, zero
dependencies, SSE and POST) but is not wired in here; this app makes no network calls at all. Both need sockets, and this app makes no network calls at all: the
dashboard holds the devices and evaluates rules against events you report. There is no multicast listener and
no "discovering…" spinner pretending otherwise.

The LAN guard
-------------

Every address the app accepts is a private address: 10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16, loopback and link-local. A
public address or a hostname is refused when it is typed, because a home dashboard has no business reaching
the internet — and since the app makes no calls, the guard is the whole of the promise rather than a check on
something it does.
